Chlorofracture

Ingredients: BREAKBEAT GARAGE & GRIME + SKA + HYPNOTIC, TRANCE-LIKE & MINIMAL + Shaker  
Creative Catalyst: Ex-botanists in the cloud forests of Quito translated the bio-electric voltage of parasitic orchids into hyper-syncopated dance music.

Chlorofracture sounds like an impossibly sped-up, bone-dry Jamaican ska skank slammed into a brutalist, sub-heavy London basement. The off-beat guitar chop is replaced by the hyper-amplified, abrasive friction of dried seeded shakers—specifically the dried seed-pods of Eperua falcata—delivering a razor-sharp, hypnotic 2-step shuffle. Over this minimalist trance-inducing pulse, ultra-distorted, low-end square wave basslines (cloned from plant stress signals) drop with the violent, staccato aggression of pure grime, while sparse, hollow-body brass stabs echo into endless sub-tropical reverberation.

Genre DNA

* Tempo & Pulse: 138–142 BPM. A hypnotic, highly syncopated 2-step garage swing where the classic ska off-beat is driven strictly by mechanical shaker arrays rather than drums, anchored by heavy, subterranean grime sub-bass drops.
* Harmonic Palette: Phrygian Dominant and Microtonal Plant-Scale mutations. Stripped-down, minimal two-chord vamps that endlessly repeat to induce trance, interrupted only by sudden pitch-bending sub-frequency slides.
* Production Signatures: 
  1. Bio-Voltage Galvanics: Oscillators modulated directly by live micro-voltage data streams from flora, creating unpredictable, twitching bass filter cutoffs.
  2. Pod-Chop Friction: Multi-tracked, close-miked plant shakers granularly shifted and hard-panned to construct a wall of high-frequency rhythmic noise.
  3. Cloud-Forest Gated Reverb: Ultra-dry, violent grime MC/vocal cuts that abruptly burst into massive, hyper-real humid space reverbs before snapping back to absolute silence.
* Dynamics: Extreme, stark minimalism that builds through relentless repetition. Tracks loop hypnotically for minutes before dropping all mid-range frequencies, leaving only an oppressive sub-bass roar and a maddening, high-speed shaker tick.

Scene & Origin Lore

Chlorofracture emerged from El Invernadero, an abandoned, humid high-altitude glasshouse on the slopes of Mount Pichincha, Ecuador, circa 2028. Founded by a fugitive collective of ethno-botanists and illegal low-power radio operators, the scene grew around illegal sound system dances held inside fogged-up, damp greenhouses. Scene followers—known as Hoja-Heads—dress in militarized, moisture-wicking Gore-Tex tracksuits dripping with condensation, carrying hand-carved shaker batons filled with dried jungle seeds. The peak of the dance ritual occurs during La Micro-Tensión, a twenty-minute stretch of a set where the light grid is cut, the bass drops to an infrasonic 24Hz, and hundreds of ravers sync their physical shakers to the trance-inducing plant-pulse in total darkness.

Key Instrumentation

 Bio-Mapped Modular Synthesizers: Custom Eurorack rigs receiving real-time biofeedback via needle electrodes clamped to living Monstera and Bromeliad* leaves.
 Seed-Pod Shaker Arrays: Heavy hand-held and mounted shakers filled with Amazonian Eperua* seeds, serving as the genre's master rhythmic clock.
* Square-Wave Sub-Bass: Grime-style, hyper-compressed square waves filtered through low-pass gates to mimic sub-soil root pressure.
* Minimal Ska-Chop Guitar: A single, heavily muted Telecaster playing ultra-staccato, bone-dry off-beat chops on every second beat.

